From 19e6f63c68b8da8f667d6866612d1019c3898af1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 08:52:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07631/11362] [outer-loop] candidate-coverage attribution:
 independent replication + bp35 generation-gap finding

Operator: "how do we reproduce the successful techniques used by the
top leaderboard projects?" -> pointed to the existing 2026-07-20
source-level winner audit (Carnot already has more search machinery
than any Milestone-1 winner; their edge is generator size +
orientation-compute + object-centric perception) and its proposed,
unrun candidate-coverage attribution experiment. Operator: "yes."

Built scripts/arc_candidate_coverage_attribution.py without first
checking ops/verifier_gaps.md -- this exact experiment already exists
(REQ-ARC-FCP-5757, 2026-07-20). Disclosed honestly rather than
hidden. The game selection (lf52/bp35/re86, this session's own worst
live/oracle-gap games) happened to be fully disjoint from 5757's 9
games, so the run became a genuine independent out-of-sample
replication rather than a wasted duplicate.

Result (N=155 progress actions, adversarial_verify.py 0-flagged):
pooled a(generation)=13.55%, b(lookahead)=0.00%, c(selection)=23.23%,
clean=63.23%. Bucket b=0 exactly matches 5757's finding on a disjoint
game set -- real corroboration the multi-step-lookahead hypothesis
has zero support (0/247 progress actions across both runs). Directly
explains why this session's whole tool-loop-lookahead investment
(REQ-ARC-WMTE-5828) kept nulling regardless of search budget.

New finding not in 5757's sample: bp35 alone accounts for all 21 of
this run's generation misses (a=36.8% for bp35 specifically, 0% for
lf52/re86) -- every miss is a click at a specific recurring grid
coordinate rich_action_candidates() never proposes, despite returning
50+ candidates at every state. A concrete, characterized instance of
the audit's own "segmentation fidelity + click-point generation
beyond object centroids" prescription, and a direct explanation for
bp35's persistent null across all five mechanisms tested this
session. Logged as GAP-ARC-BP35-CLICK-CANDIDATE-GENERATION-MISS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
